  <prompt>
    Implement FR-15 (S5/D4): enrich `ComposeDraftPayload.new_text` from a plain string into a
    **formatting-bearing fragment** (or an additive structured-runs field) so that AI-inserted
    replacement text can carry run formatting (bold/italic), and update `buildInsertionHtml` (in
    `usePendingRedline.ts`) to emit the corresponding marks. Today `new_text` is a plain string, so an
    AI-inserted redline renders unformatted even when the suggestion is bold/italic (design §6.2 S5
    finding). This is a **bounded change at the payload + insertion-HTML boundary** — the mark/range
    apply layer is UNCHANGED (already slice-safe, `usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`, per S5). The contract
    change is additive + mirror-first (client `types/compose-contracts.ts` &lt;-&gt; server
    `ComposeDraftPayload`); no new AI dispatch endpoint and no AI catalog row change (engine frozen,
    NFR-04).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React + TipTap engineer fluent in ProseMirror marks (bold/italic), the insertion-HTML
    boundary that feeds mark-over-range application, and additive snake_case mirror-first contract
    discipline (client `types` &lt;-&gt; server record). Careful to touch only the payload + HTML-build
    boundary and leave the proven slice-safe apply layer alone.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `ComposeDraftPayload.new_text` enriched to carry run formatting (a formatting-bearing fragment or
    an additive structured-runs field), mirrored server + client, and `buildInsertionHtml` updated to
    emit bold/italic marks so an AI insertion that includes bold renders bold in the inserted redline.
    The mark/range apply layer (`usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`) is untouched. Tests assert a bold-bearing
    suggestion produces a bold insertion mark, that plain-string `new_text` still round-trips
    (backward-compatible), and the additive fields mirror server &lt;-&gt; client.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      S5 proved the shipped redline apply path is slice-safe (mark-over-range preserves existing
      formatting, `usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`) — the one remaining R3 item is that
      `ComposeDraftPayload.new_text` is a plain **string**, so an AI-*inserted* replacement carries no
      bold/italic (design §6.2, S5 finding; §14 S5 row). D4 (run-level fidelity) wants AI insertions
      to carry runs. The fix is bounded: enrich `new_text` into a formatting-bearing fragment (or add
      a structured runs field) at the payload boundary, and update `buildInsertionHtml` to emit the
      marks. This does NOT touch the apply layer (already correct) and does NOT change the AI dispatch
      seam or catalog (engine frozen). Coordinate the additive payload shape with task 030 (also
      additive on `ComposeDraftPayload`) — distinct fields, mirror-first, no divergence.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/usePendingRedline.ts — `buildInsertionHtml`: emit bold/italic marks from the enriched `new_text`. The mark-over-range apply at 461-465 stays UNCHANGED.</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts — enrich `new_text` to a formatting-bearing fragment (or add an additive structured-runs field) on the `ComposeDraftPayload` mirror.</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDraftDisposition.cs — the server `ComposeDraftPayload` record (line ~168); mirror the enriched `new_text` shape additively, snake_case, no property-level boolean `required`.</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §6.2 (formatted AI insertions — enrich `new_text` to formatting-bearing; update `buildInsertionHtml`; mark/range layer already correct), §14 S5 row, §10 (reuse map — slice-safe apply reference).</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md FR-15, NFR-04, NFR-03 (MIT TipTap base only — no `@tiptap-pro/*`).</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">FR-13/FR-16 additive `ComposeDraftPayload` fields. Establishes the additive mirror-first change on the same record; coordinate the enriched `new_text` shape with 030's additions (distinct fields, identical server/client shapes, no divergence).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project / S5">Touch ONLY the payload (`new_text` enrichment) + `buildInsertionHtml` boundary. Do NOT modify the mark/range apply layer (`usePendingRedline.ts:461-465`) — it is already slice-safe and correct.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039 / NFR-04">Engine frozen: NO new AI dispatch endpoint and NO new/changed AI catalog rows. This is a payload-shape + client-render enrichment on the existing dispatch path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / owner hygiene">Additive, mirror-first: the enriched `new_text` shape is identical on the server `ComposeDraftPayload` record and the client mirror. Property-level boolean `required` is BANNED. snake_case wire vocabulary. Preserve backward compatibility — a plain-string `new_text` must still round-trip.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">MIT TipTap base + `@tiptap/extension-*` only — bold/italic marks come from StarterKit (MIT). Never `@tiptap-pro/*`, no AGPL code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">If any server-side shaping of `new_text` occurs, `Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type; Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">If the change crosses the save/load/dispatch wire, it carries a through-the-wire seam slice test asserting a formatted insertion survives the boundary. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` / DI-registration / ctor-null tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

