  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Confirm task 030's additive changes to `ComposeDraftPayload` (coordinate the shared record). Run the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load `bff-extensions.md` + the ADR knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Enrich the `new_text` shape (mirror-first)">Enrich `new_text` on the client mirror (`compose-contracts.ts`) and the server record (`ComposeDraftDisposition.cs`) to a formatting-bearing fragment (or add an additive structured-runs field). Keep it additive + backward-compatible (plain string still valid), snake_case, no boolean `required`.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Emit marks in `buildInsertionHtml`">Update `buildInsertionHtml` in `usePendingRedline.ts` to translate the enriched `new_text` into HTML carrying bold/italic marks (StarterKit MIT marks). Do NOT modify the mark/range apply at 461-465.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Tests">Author tests asserting: a bold-bearing suggestion yields a bold insertion mark in the rendered redline; a plain-string `new_text` still round-trips unchanged (backward compatibility); the enriched shape mirrors server &lt;-&gt; client. If the change crosses the wire, add/extend a through-the-wire seam slice test.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify">Build the client shared lib (+ BFF if the record changed); run the tests. If BFF touched: report publish size delta + CVE + NetArchTest facade. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

